// spec: VAR-011
//
// A section is a feature of a HEADER.  At the top level 'var' declares exactly
// one name, and the run of declarations beneath it is read as ordinary
// statements.
//
// ⚠️ LABELS CHANGED HOW THIS IS REFUSED, and the diagnostic got worse.  'B :'
// is now read as a label [STM-010] on the statement 'String;', so the line
// parses and fails at run time rather than at parse time.  The program is still
// refused; what is lost is that it used to be caught without being run.  This
// is the price of a label needing no keyword, and it is the only place in the
// language where the two forms collide.

var A : Integer;
    B : String;
